    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mze7rbg2fc2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "If this holds up, it is big: \"We asked GPT-6 Astra to edit Qwen3.5-0.8B weights to improve math. It directly changed only 0.016% of weights, fixing 0.8B's reasoning loops & improving math up to 6x and even instruction following 3x, without gradients or training.\" rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mze7rbg2fc2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-02T21:00:10.481Z",
      "likes": 251,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 36,
      "score": 7.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.5,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 23.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzesndbbxs2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Here is a mass attempted replication of old findings of LLMs with new models. Much conventional wisdom is outdated.\n\nRecent models no longer invent citations and both hallucination rates & stereotyping has dropped. But they are still sycophantic & lean left.  zou-group.github.io/llm-claims-s...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzesndbbxs2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-03T02:37:59.273Z",
      "likes": 163,
      "replies": 16,
      "reposts": 24,
      "score": 7.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 17.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzdotrufck2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "When you think about the Labs' weird approach to software releases (sudden changes, bad communication), it is worth remembering that a core belief is that these products are a temporary thing they have to do to raise money for a couple years until \"true\" AGI makes all products obsolete.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzdotrufck2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-02T15:57:21.227Z",
      "likes": 75,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 6.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 28.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:vtpyqvwce4x6gpa5dcizqecy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzgbe66k6l2r",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Google will let schools disable its AI tools, but not without sacrificing Search",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzgbe66k6l2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-03T16:33:57.000Z",
      "likes": 18,
      "replies": 10,
      "reposts": 5,
      "score": 6.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.6,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 3.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzfxdpidi42i",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I'll also note that this appears to largely be one-shotting the weight edits. When combined with RL or evolutionary search loops, this should mean that specialized neural networks can be built without back propagation on data. This is where things will get really interesting.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzfxdpidi42i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-03T13:34:45.016Z",
      "likes": 5,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 6.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzfxdpnx642i",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Aside: In 2018 @matthewguz.bsky.social and I were playing around with direct manipulation of neural nets without backprop arxiv.org/abs/1802.03605. Didn't work super well, but the models were crude by today's standards. Fun to see things we were trying in 2018 might actually work quite well today.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzfxdpnx642i",
